# Check TypeScript and Svelte Errors

After any change to TypeScript or Svelte code, **verify before finishing**:

1. **IDE diagnostics** — Run ReadLints on every file you edited.
2. **Svelte** — For `.svelte` / `.svelte.ts` / `.svelte.js` changes, run `svelte-autofixer` (Svelte MCP) and keep fixing until clean. Also run:
   ```bash
   pnpm --filter @ai-v-models/web exec svelte-check --threshold error
   ```
   Fix errors in files you touched (or that your change broke). Do not ignore new errors.
3. **TypeScript** — For package/backend changes, typecheck the affected package:
   ```bash
   pnpm --filter @ai-v-models/proxy exec tsc --noEmit
   pnpm --filter @ai-v-models/web exec tsc --noEmit
   ```
4. **Runtime** — If the app is running, check the dev terminal for compile/proxy errors (e.g. ECONNREFUSED → API 500s) and confirm the changed route loads.

## exactOptionalPropertyTypes

This repo uses `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`. Do **not** assign `undefined` to optional fields:

```ts
// ❌ BAD
{ api_key: apiKey || undefined, latency_ms: value ?? undefined }

// ✅ GOOD
{ ...(apiKey ? { api_key: apiKey } : {}) }
if (value != null) obj.latency_ms = value;
```

## Do not finish with known errors

If checks fail for your changes, fix them in the same turn. Pre-existing errors in unrelated files may remain, but call them out if you notice them.
